Let razerkbd and razermouse drive HyperFlux Next virtual devices

HyperFlux Next presents each wireless Razer device paired to a HyperFlux
V2 receiver as a uhid device with a single 90-byte feature report. Its
device keeper creates the device, and the bridge answers the reports.
With this change the two drivers bind such a device and send it the
reports they would send over USB, as a feature SET and GET.

A virtual device is only taken when it is on the virtual bus, from
vendor 0x1532, with HyperFlux Next's phys prefix and report descriptor,
and with a product id the driver already lists for USB. HyperFlux Next's
udev rules leave /dev/uhid to the hyperflux-keeper group.

The bridge reports a missing response in-band ("HFXNERR1"). The drivers
return it as EAGAIN (not sent) or ENOTRECOVERABLE (may have been sent), a
mismatched response as ENOTRECOVERABLE, and for these devices the sysfs
handlers return the first error instead of ignoring it.

Nothing sends the device-mode command or touches autosuspend without a
USB device. Both modules carry hyperflux_native_transport, as a modinfo
tag and as a read-only parameter.

99-razer.rules gains bind-time rules, since its USB-based rules never
match a virtual device. The group stays plugdev; packaging substitutes
it.

Applies to OpenRazer 3.12.4 (1ef8a91712906a89fd332a2ed62bbd105315d6d1).

